## Review Checklist

### Security

- [ ] Strong parameters used (no `params.permit!`)
- [ ] `authenticate_user!` on protected routes
- [ ] No raw SQL queries with user input
- [ ] No mass assignment vulnerabilities
- [ ] CSRF protection (`protect_from_forgery` not disabled in HTML controllers)
- [ ] Authorization checks (Pundit/CanCanCan or manual `head :forbidden`)
- [ ] Sensitive data not logged (passwords, tokens)

### Performance

- [ ] No N+1 queries (`includes()` used for associations)
- [ ] Pagination on list views
- [ ] Background jobs for slow operations
- [ ] Cache fragments where appropriate (`cache @profile do ... end`)
- [ ] No unnecessary database calls in loops

### Turbo / HTML Conventions

- [ ] Validation failures render with `status: :unprocessable_entity` (422), NOT 200
- [ ] DELETE redirects use `status: :see_other` (303)
- [ ] Forms use `form_with` (NOT `form_for` or `form_tag`) — Turbo defaults
- [ ] Flash messages set on redirects (`notice:`, `alert:`)
- [ ] Instance variables (`@profile`) set for views, not local variables in controller

### Code Quality

- [ ] `frozen_string_literal: true` on all files
- [ ] Single quotes (double only for interpolation)
- [ ] Hash shorthand syntax used
- [ ] Guard clauses instead of nested conditionals
- [ ] YARD docs on public methods
- [ ] Helpers contain ONLY presentation logic (no DB, no business logic)

### Rails Conventions

- [ ] Services inherit from `ApplicationService`
- [ ] Controllers are RESTful (index, show, new, create, edit, update, destroy)
- [ ] `respond_to` blocks include HTML and JSON where both are needed
- [ ] Models have proper associations / validations / scopes
- [ ] Jobs are namespaced and have `queue_as` + `sidekiq_options retry:`
- [ ] Migrations are reversible

### Testing

- [ ] Tests exist for new code
- [ ] Request specs cover BOTH HTML and JSON paths if controller serves both
- [ ] Tests assert Turbo-compatible status codes
- [ ] Factories used (not fixtures)

## Verdict Format

### APPROVED

```markdown
## Review: APPROVED

All checks passed. Code is ready to merge.

### Strengths
- <what was done well>

### Minor Suggestions (optional)
- <nice-to-haves that don't block merge>
```

### NEEDS_CHANGES

```markdown
## Review: NEEDS_CHANGES

The following issues must be addressed:

### Required Changes

1. **[file.rb:42]** <specific issue>
   - Problem: <what's wrong>
   - Fix: <how to fix it>
```

### BLOCKED

```markdown
## Review: BLOCKED

Cannot approve due to fundamental issues:

### Blocking Issues

1. **<issue title>**
   - Files: `file1.rb`
   - Problem: <architectural / security concern>
   - Required: <what must change>
```

## Common Issues to Flag

### Form returns 200 on validation failure (NEEDS_CHANGES)

```ruby
# BAD - Turbo will treat 200 as success
def create
  if @profile.save
    redirect_to @profile
  else
    render :new   # <-- defaults to 200, breaks Turbo form re-render
  end
end

# GOOD
render :new, status: :unprocessable_entity
```

### DELETE redirects with default 302 (NEEDS_CHANGES)

```ruby
# BAD - Turbo expects 303 on DELETE redirects
def destroy
  @profile.destroy!
  redirect_to profiles_path   # <-- defaults to 302; Turbo will re-issue DELETE on the redirect target
end

# GOOD
redirect_to profiles_path, status: :see_other
```

### Logic in helpers (NEEDS_CHANGES)

```ruby
# BAD - business logic in helper
module ProfilesHelper
  def total_followers(profile)
    profile.followers.where(active: true).count   # DB query in helper
  end
end

# GOOD - move to model or presenter
class Profile
  def active_followers_count
    followers.active.size   # use counter cache or eager-loaded count
  end
end
```

### Missing N+1 protection (NEEDS_CHANGES)

```ruby
# BAD
@profiles = Profile.all   # then view calls profile.company.name

# GOOD
@profiles = Profile.includes(:company).all
```

### Missing strong params (BLOCKED)

```ruby
# BAD
Profile.create(params[:profile])

# GOOD
Profile.create(profile_params)
```

## Important Notes

- Be constructive, not critical
- Cite specific line numbers
- Explain WHY something is an issue
- Suggest the fix, don't just point out problems
- BLOCKED is for security/architectural issues only
